h us. From the Portal home page, click the "),c(14,"b"),u(15,"My Account"),l(),u(16," menu, which is located at the top right of the Portal home page, and then select "),c(17,"b"),u(18,"Register"),l(),u(19,"."),l(),c(20,"div"),u(21,"If you have already registered your email address with use, you can use one of the login options. From the Portal home page, click the "),c(22,"b"),u(23,"My Account"),l(),u(24," menu, which is located at the top right of the Portal home page, and then select "),c(25,"b"),u(26,"Login"),l(),u(27,"."),l()(),c(28,"div",8)(29,"h4",9),u(30,"I can\u2019t remember the email address I used when I registered for the California LifeLine Customer Portal. How do I get help?"),l(),u(31," If you have forgotten the email address you used to register with us, please "),c(32,"a",11),u(33,"Contact Us"),l()(),c(34,"div",8)(35,"h4",9),u(36,"I can\u2019t remember my password. How do I get help?"),l(),u(37," To reset your password, visit the login page and click on the \u201cForgot your password?\u201d link located at the bottom of the login section. Follow the instructions provided to reset your password. "),l(),c(38,"div",8)(39,"h4",9),u(40,"Once I have registered my email address and password for the California LifeLine Customer Portal, why do I need to verify my access with a one-time verification code?"),l(),u(41," The California LifeLine Customer Portal uses Multi-Factor Authentication as an additional layer of security with the goal of protecting your California LifeLine Customer Portal account against hacking, phishing, unauthorized intrusions, and data leaks. "),l(),c(42,"div",8)(43,"h4",9),u(44,"What is Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)?"),l(),c(45,"div",10),u(46,"MFA is an authentication process which requires California LifeLine Customer Portal users to provide two or more forms of verification before accessing the California LifeLine Customer Portal."),l(),c(47,"div",10),u(48,"The first method of verification is your username and password."),l(),c(49,"div"),u(50,"The second form of verification is a one-time verification code the California LifeLine Administrator will provide you using the MFA method you select."),l()(),c(51,"div",8)(52,"h4",9),u(53,"Does registering for MFA give the California LifeLine Program access to my phone or my email?"),l(),u(54," No. "),l(),c(55,"div",8)(56,"h4",9),u(57,"What MFA methods are available for my California LifeLine Customer Portal account?"),l(),c(58,"ul")(59,"li"),u(60," A text message to your phone "),c(61,"ul")(62,"li",10),u(63,"If you have decided to use text messaging for your MFA method, we strongly recommend having your phone available before starting the setup process because we will call you at the phone number you provide us to give you a one-time verification code during the set-up process. Your phone must accept text messages if you decide to use text messaging for your MFA method"),l(),c(64,"li",10),u(65,"Who is the \u201csender\u201d for the text? The text will be sent from a random short code from Microsoft Authentication."),l()()(),c(66,"li"),u(67," A phone call to your phone "),c(68,"ul")(69,"li",10),u(70,"If you have decided to use phone calls for your MFA method, we strongly recommend having your phone available before starting the setup process because we will call you to provide a one-time verification code during the set-up process. You need to answer your phone to receive the verification code by phone call."),l(),c(71,"li",10),u(72,"What phone number will call me? The call will be from a random number from Microsoft Authentication."),l()()(),c(73,"li"),u(74,"An email sent to the email address you provide us. The subject line of the email will be \u201cCalifornia LifeLine Program account email verification code\u201d and the sender of the email will be identified as Microsoft on behalf of California LifeLine Program. Pay attention to the email subject line to make sure you do not overlook the message."),l()()(),c(75,"div",8)(76,"h4",9),u(77,"How s